<title>AZERBAIJAN: Azerbaijan's Azal launching Baku-Paris route.</title>
<headline>Azerbaijan's Azal launching Baku-Paris route.</headline>
<dateline>BAKU 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Azeri state airline Azal will launch regular Baku-Paris passenger flights from July 1, a company spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>Magerram Safarli said that Azal would operate an Airbus A-310 twice a week.</p>
<p>He also said Azal had permission from Air France to sell tickets on routes from Baku to Washington, Houston and New York via Paris where passengers from Azerbaijan will transfer to Air France aircraft.</p>
<p>Safarli said that Air France officials would shortly visit Baku to sign documents on cooperation between thhe two carriers.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
